  "task": "In one Part Design body, create a cylindrical blank with radius 22 mm and height 36 mm, centered on the global Z axis, with its bottom face on the XY plane at Z = 0 and its top face at Z = 36. Create the subtractive-helix cutter profile as a new circle sketch on the XZ plane, facing along the Y direction, with radius 2 mm and center at global coordinates (22, 0, 0) so the circle straddles the cylinder side wall. Use Part Design Subtractive Helix around the global Z axis with 3 turns, 12 mm pitch, height 36 mm, and 0 degree cone angle to cut one helical groove around the cylinder. Keep FreeCAD's default feature names ('Cylinder' for the additive cylinder, 'Sketch' for the circle sketch, 'SubtractiveHelix'), and fully constrain the circle sketch. Save the completed model to /home/user/Unnamed.FCStd.",
